  One of the things #ScenarioPlanning taught me is that the future rarely unfolds as a clean “replacement” of a previous set of conditions. Instead, it tends to emerge as a kind of overlay, coexisting for some time with the present.
  
  Technical capability appears first. Then adoption follows, but unevenly. Regulation lags along behind.
  
  Human behavior adapts to the changes in unpredictable ways.
  That’s why I’m less interested in when a profession will “die” & more interested in how its value and focus evolve across different possible futures.
  
  Curious to hear how you see this playing out in your field.
  
