  24
  The most valuable technique to learn may be how to draft effective prompts, known by the
  25
  erudite label prompt engineering. This skill is probably the most helpful one to acquire over
  the next several years for using AI productively. Prompt engineering entails familiar skills for
  lawyers of asking clear, tailored questions with follow-up ones although questions customized
  for AI inquiries. An effective prompt at this juncture should specify the parameters of an inquiry
  such as context (e.g., for planning, a transaction, judicial setting, etc), audience (e.g., for a judge,
  client, students, CLE program, etc), relevant facts, any restrictions and guardrails (what NOT
  want AI to do so less likely to go rogue), links for sources, and desired output (e.g., checklist,
  chart, memo, draft a document, etc). Learning proficient prompting requires awareness, training,
  experience, and trial-and-error.
  
  Suitable prompts can reduce the risks of hallucinations, errors and uninformed AI judgments.
  For example, a user who wants to reduce the risks of hallucinations might instruct a bot to
  answer a question by specifying in the prompt that: Any answer must rely exclusively on the
  content of attached contract and should not draw upon any information outside the four corners
  of the contract. Any legal points should include links to cites. In an effort to reduce risks of
  uninformed AI judgments when summarizing, the user might further specify in the prompt:
  When summarizing the contract, be sure to identify any provisions that might limit either party’s
  ability to seek damages if the contract is breached.
  
