  # [How Creative Lawyers Are Rewriting the Rules With AI](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=asT1ARvl5b8)
  
  **Visibility**: Public
  **Uploaded by**: [AI and the Future of Law Podcast](http://www.youtube.com/@AIandtheFutureofLawPodcast)
  **Uploaded at**: 2026-02-10T01:00:04-08:00
  **Published at**: 2026-02-10T01:00:04-08:00
  **Length**: 39:48
  **Views**: 585
  **Likes**: 17
  **Category**: People & Blogs
  
  ## Description
  
  ```
  AI is no longer just a research assistant for lawyers. It is becoming a collaborator.
  
  In this episode of AI and the Future of Law, Jen Leonard and Bridget McCormack break down Claude Code, agentic AI, and the rise of “vibe coding” in legal practice. 
  
  They explore how creative associates at major law firms are building real AI tools to solve everyday problems, without waiting for firm-wide mandates or formal technical training. The conversation also examines what this shift means for junior lawyers, law firm culture, billing models, and the future of legal education.
  
  Key topics include:
  - Claude Code and agentic AI systems
  - Vibe coding and low-barrier innovation
  - Creative associates driving firm-wide change
  - AI’s impact on junior legal work
  - Cultural barriers to experimentation in law
  
  Subscribe for more on AI and the Future of Law
  Listen on Spotify, Apple Podcasts & more:
  
  AAA: https://www.adr.org/podcasts/ai-and-the-future-of-law/
  PLI: https://www.pli.edu/catalog/podcasts/ai-and-the-future-of-the-law
  Spotify: https://open.spotify.com/show/2eavMpnebcCHG3Y86oXIeD
  Apple Podcasts: https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/ai-and-the-future-of-law/id1751625159
  #AIinLaw #LegalTech #ClaudeAI #FutureOfWork #ChatGPT
  ```
  
